John M. Bozeman <jmb5b@faraday.clas.virginia.edu> wrote:
>I think another possible way to increase the information available
>to NMR/MRI is through the use of radioactive tags... 

This isn't necessary.  NMR is tunable, by altering the frequency at
which you emit pulses in the magnetic field.  In fact, all the NMR
work I've done (in college) was using this to determine the composition
of unknown solutions.

You could easily build an NMR setup that scanned through the relevent
frequencies to pick up all the desired elements and isotopes.  The
only problem I can see (as far as mapping the chemistry, that is) is
that it won't pick up the "handedness" of various molecules.
