Subject: [#94-10-58] Interface .....

The interface can be described as the boundary between two or more systems
. The Art of the Interface is to ~remove~ the boundary and this can be
applied to a boundary of any kind .

If for example , you are learning to drive a car , the first stages will
be that of seperated systems : The gears , brakes , steering and
observation . As the ~user~ becomes more experienced , and this can be
applied to a user of any desccription , the separate sections merge
together .... the act of driving becomes an art ,  boundarys are
fused and the interface becomes transparent . Mind and machine are fused
. The vehicle shell becomes an extension of the body .

As we enter the next Millenium the boundary can be seen to be at the edge
of disappearing , the boundaries are being replaced by fusion .The
boudaries between natural and artificial , human and machine , real life
and virtual reality .

I am currently writing a paper on the art of the interface ,
all opinions and comments are welcome

